From: Reinhard Tartler <siretart@tauware.de>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 16:11:14 -0400
Subject: Disable flaky TestEndpointsSlicesDiscoveryWithUpdatedNodeMetadata

TestEndpointsSlicesDiscoveryWithUpdatedNodeMetadata updates a node label
from "us-east1" to "us-central1", but its assertion incorrectly still
expects the old "us-east1" label.

If the update event arrives before the test's 1-second timeout expires
(as observed on s390x in Debian CI), the test fails with a label mismatch.

Skip the test in Debian package builds until upstream fixes the test.

Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1135688
Forwarded: not-needed
---
 discovery/kubernetes/endpointslice_test.go | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/discovery/kubernetes/endpointslice_test.go b/discovery/kubernetes/endpointslice_test.go
index 9eea9ab..cd236a2 100644
--- a/discovery/kubernetes/endpointslice_test.go
+++ b/discovery/kubernetes/endpointslice_test.go
@@ -730,6 +730,7 @@ func TestEndpointsSlicesDiscoveryWithNodeMetadata(t *testing.T) {
 }
 
 func TestEndpointsSlicesDiscoveryWithUpdatedNodeMetadata(t *testing.T) {
+	t.Skip("Disabled for Debian build: timing race between node update and discovery timeout, see Debian #1135688")
 	t.Parallel()
 	metadataConfig := AttachMetadataConfig{Node: true}
 	nodeLabels1 := map[string]string{"az": "us-east1"}
